\ Regression test for per-quotation lexical scope surviving a value deep copy.
\
\ A spawned task defines a local word `secret`, curries a closure that closes over
\ it, and leaves that closure as its result. `await` deep-copies the result into
\ this task, which has no `secret` binding of its own. The closure must still
\ resolve `secret` to its creation-site value through the scope carried on the
\ closure value; a deep copy that dropped the scope would resolve `secret` against
\ this task's frames and fail with an unknown word.
\
\ This exercises the deep-copy boundary (`await` / channel send), distinct from the
\ spawn-input boundary the sibling closure-capture tests cover.

use "testing" ;

[
  \ await path: the closure is the task's deep-copied result.
  [ secret: 7 ; 10 [ secret + ] curry ] spawn
  await call 17 "curried closure over a local survives await's deep copy" assert=

  \ channel path: the closure is deep-copied on send and called in another task.
  reply: 1 <buffered-channel> ;
  handoff: 1 <buffered-channel> ;

  [ handoff receive call reply send ] spawn

  [ boost: 100 ; 5 [ boost + ] curry handoff send ] call
  reply receive 105 "curried closure over a local survives a channel send" assert=
] task-scope

"deep-copy-scope" print-line
